        },
        "quote": "The following words, terms and phrases, when used in this chapter, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:0#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.55.010 block 1",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "7e54b10a-cf66-5f7e-aa69-6bd4e17b4888",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 606,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:1",
          "start": 189
        },
        "quote": "“Snow tire” means a tire which, when compared with conventional rib type tires, has a relatively aggressive tread pattern and is designed primarily to provide additional starting, stopping and driving traction in snow, and shall have a tread depth of at least four thirty-seconds of an inch. The tread has ribs, lugs, blocks or buttons; is generally discontinuous, and has the following characteristics when inflated:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.55.010 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "8d14f935-60c0-51c6-ba01-ce3be849dc9d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 763,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:2",
          "start": 607
        },
        "quote": "(1) A substantial portion of the lug, block or rib edges in the tread design are at an angle greater than 30 degrees to the tire circumferential centerline.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.55.010 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "1a84ac40-1362-5bc8-b4e8-08497fb72a46",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 926,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:3",
          "start": 764
        },
        "quote": "(2) On at least one side of the tread design, the shoulder lugs protrude at least one-half inch in a direction generally perpendicular to the direction of travel.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.55.010 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "b1ba5baa-282b-5c2d-b0ec-d6097fffe05d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1115,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:4",
          "start": 927
        },
        "quote": "(3) Tires, as defined above, manufactured after January 1, 1976, will be permanently labeled on one sidewall with the words “MUD and SNOW” or any contraction using the letters “M” and “S.”",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.55.010 block 5",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 5,
          "component_id": "da9faee2-5169-57b5-9ea3-2f16e6c89a20",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1290,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:5",
          "start": 1116
        },
        "quote": "“Tire chain” means a device which, when attached to the tires, provides additional starting, stopping and driving traction in snow. (Code 1981 § 43-289. Code 1995 § 142-536.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.55.010:block:5#text",
